      "snippet": "[Letterboxd Review of \"The Accountant\"] “Let’s just say that one day, your grandchildren will be eatin’ cornbread that’s sweet and drinkin’ iced tea that ain’t…”Such a sharp, dark, funny, and dry satirical narrative short. So cynical as to feel like the 90s but way ahead of its time when you realize this was made in 2001. Writer-director-star Ray McKinnon is incredible as the double-talking, straight-faced, conspiracy theorist accountant. He walks around the farm chugging PBRs in a Men in Black suit, donning mutton chop sideburns and a southern accent so thick I’m glad I used subtitles. He is so good that this might as well have bee",
